WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.650
From action throwbacks to kid-friendly fare,
hard-hitting dramas to game-changing horror,

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.519
this year has already delivered a bumper crop
of excellent flicks for film lovers.

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:14.249
We're still just a few pages into the calendar,
but let's take a quick look back at the best

00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:16.640
movies of 2017 so far.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.550
The LEGO Batman Movie

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.779
Trying to follow up The LEGO Movie was a tough
proposition, and spinning off Will Arnett's

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:25.990
Batman into his own movie could easily have
backfired.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:29.759
The filmmakers could've faltered under the
pressure of making this Batman likable or

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:34.340
interesting enough to carry his own film — or
buckled under the weight of all those DC Comics

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.559
in-jokes and gags ...

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:42.320
"Crazy Quilt, Eraser, Polka Dot Man, Mime,
Tarantula, King Tut, Orca, Killer Moth, March

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.340
Harriet, Zodiac Master, Gentleman Ghost..."

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.370
Happily, The LEGO Batman Movie turned out
to be one of the best family-friendly movies

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:52.859
in ages, while packing in enough smart comic
stuff to keep Batman geeks coming back for

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:53.870
repeat viewings.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.579
Fun, wacky, and a rollicking adventure in
the wild world of LEGO, the movie's been showered

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:02.590
with praise from critics who are calling it
one of the best animated offerings of the

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.320
year — and one of the best Batman movies
ever.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.060
John Wick: Chapter 2

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:13.150
More than 15 years after The Matrix saga began,
Keanu Reeves has reinvented himself as an

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.650
action hero for a whole new generation.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:20.150
This sequel to his surprise 2014 action hit
John Wick is a bone-crushing, R-rated thrill

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:25.320
ride that finds Reeves' namesake hitman pulled
out of retirement to take on a shady international

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.320
conspiracy.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.860
"So I guess you have a choice.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:34.150
Do you want a war, or do you just want to
just give me a gun?"

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.250
Sure, it's mostly just a setup for Reeves
to kick — and shoot — a bunch of bad-guy

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.250
butt.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.980
Critics, however, say the film feels like
a throwback to the simpler days of action

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.810
films, focusing on practical effects instead
of distracting CGI.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.040
It's also one of the most stylish films of
the year, regardless of genre.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.620
Hidden Figures

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.090
This historical drama technically opened late
in 2016, but didn't go wide until this year.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:02.630
It tells the inspiring true story of the black
women who worked at NASA during the early

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:07.150
days of the U.S. space program, and the critical
roles they played in helping America with

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.630
the space race.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:13.739
Stars Taraji P. Henson, Octavia Spencer, and
Janelle Monáe did a fantastic job of bringing

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:18.659
this era to life while lending genuine emotional
heft to the film's portrayal of their struggles

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:19.659
and triumphs.

00:02:19.659 --> 00:02:25.290
Not only is it a fascinating real-life story
— it's uplifting and all-around entertaining.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.180
Patriots Day

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.670
Director Peter Berg's dramatic retelling of
the real-life 2013 Boston Marathon bombing

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.400
stars Mark Wahlberg, making this his third
fact-based thriller with Berg.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.340
Wahlberg plays a police sergeant thrust into
the middle of the chaos and the ensuing investigation

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.469
of the bombing.

00:02:42.469 --> 00:02:46.841
Critics have praised Patriots Day, which also
opened in limited release late in 2016, for

00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:51.140
managing to tell a compelling story without
exploiting the real-life tragedy.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.930
While some reviews question whether it's too
soon to bring this particular story to the

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:59.310
cineplex, there's no denying it finds Berg
and Wahlberg in their wheelhouse … and lets

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.209
Wahlberg be Boston as all get-out:

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:03.960
"You gotta start lettin' Boston workin' for
us, I'm tellin' ya."

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:06.300
Split

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:10.980
Pretty much no one saw it coming, but M. Night
Shyamalan's surprise hit, Split, is among

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.730
the best films of the year.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.810
The taut thriller follows a group of young
women abducted by a man, played by James McAvoy,

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:18.849
with multiple personalities.

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:24.030
And those personalities' struggle for dominance
threaten to upend his plans…or make things

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.069
even worse for his captives.

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:30.160
Critics have hailed it as an unexpected return
to form for the writer/director, and a big

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.670
part of the film's buzz comes from Shyamalan's
traditional big twist in the final act.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.470
And it isn't just the shocking fact that the
twist is actually good this time that makes

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.300
Split so much fun, either.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.920
McAvoy ties it all together with a tour de
force performance.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.079
The Founder

00:03:45.079 --> 00:03:49.840
This true-story tale follows Ray Kroc, played
by Michael Keaton, and the twisty real-life

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.020
saga of how the McDonald's fast-food chain
was born.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:57.250
For those who've never stopped to consider
the Big Mac's origin story, it's a surprisingly

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.430
timely tale that delves into the dark side
of the American Dream.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.260
"I just cannot stop thinking about this tremendous
restaurant!"

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.900
Critics have praised Keaton for his multifaceted
performance.

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:11.640
And while some have noted that the movie could
have dug a little deeper, it all goes down

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.610
about as easy as a Micky D's shake...

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:17.200
"Do they have Krusty partially gelatinated,
non-dairy gum-based beverages?"

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.200
"Mmm hmmm…

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.670
They call them shakes."

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:20.670
"Shakes?

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.400
You don't know what you're getting."

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.400
Get Out

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.680
Point to a February horror movie on your average
release calendar, and you're probably singling

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.200
out a pretty lame film.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.920
but there's always an exception.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.760
This year, Get Out is that amazing exception.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.370
Helmed by first-time feature director Jordan
Peele of Key &amp; Peele fame …

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.080
"Everybody here gets to design their own gremlin."

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.240
… this horror/comedy hybrid follows the
increasingly frightening misadventures of

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.170
a young man venturing into the suburbs to
meet his girlfriend's parents.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:56.350
They have no idea he's black until he arrives,
which feeds into the film's creeping tension…but

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.540
of course, that's only the start.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:04.240
Thrilling as it is thought-provoking, this
is one 2017 movie no film buff will want to

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.240
miss.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.240
Logan

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.570
Comics fans have loved Wolverine for decades,
partly because the character has a dark, violent

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.230
streak a mile wide.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:16.640
And although Hugh Jackman has played the X-Man
just about perfectly, none of those outings

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:21.110
have truly captured the grueling angst and
berserker rage that help make his saga so

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.110
poignant.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:26.480
That all changes with Logan, a loose adaptation
of the Old Man Logan comic book story that

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.180
finds our hero in a grim wasteland, called
upon to defend a mysterious girl targeted

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.170
by a pack of bloodthirsty villains.

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:38.140
A brooding Western road trip with claws, Logan's
been hailed by critics as a fitting farewell

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:43.260
for Jackman — and perhaps the best entry
in the X-Men franchise to date.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.970
Kong: Skull Island

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:49.410
It's been a long time coming, but Warner Bros.
and Legendary Pictures knocked it out of the

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.810
park with the new-look version of King Kong
in Skull Island.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:56.970
The story follows a team of explorers and
soldiers as they head off to a mysterious

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.240
island...that turns out to be the home of
giant monsters.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:03.870
Critics have been raving about the A-list
cast, praising the aesthetics of the 1970s

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:08.910
setting, and saying it strikes the perfect
balance of big stakes, dumb fun, and wildly

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.450
enjoyable action.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.260
"I call 'em skull crawlers…"

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:12.760
"Why?"

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.380
"Never said that name out loud before.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.030
It sounds stupid now that I said it.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:18.530
You call 'em whatever you want."

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:22.880
It also looks to set the stage for an eventual
crossover with Godzilla that'll set up the

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.530
studio's MonsterVerse.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.500
Skull Island is only the beginning.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:31.970
With luck, we'll finally get that modern reboot
of the greatest monster story ever told: Godzilla's

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.080
journey to become a great dad.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.550
Thanks for watching!

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.400
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.770
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love!

